Implement module ordered_retire with clk,rst_n and ports {"inputs": [["flush", 1], ["issue", 1], ["issue_tag", 2], ["finish", 1], ["finish_tag", 2]], "outputs": [["count", 2], ["retired", 1], ["retired_tag", 2]]}
Specification:
Two-slot ordered retirement queue with distinct 2-bit tags. Async active-low reset clears all state and outputs. Only rising edges act. flush has priority: clear queue and retired_tag and retired pulse. Otherwise retired is one iff the OLD head exists and was already finished; retire that head and update retired_tag, else retired=0 and hold retired_tag. finish marks any OLD queued matching tag finished; unknown tags ignored, and a just-issued tag cannot finish on that same edge. issue appends unfinished issue_tag iff OLD count<2 and issue_tag differs from all OLD queued tags; otherwise ignored. A full OLD queue rejects issue even when retiring; an OLD duplicate rejects issue even if that tag retires. Accepted issue appends after survivors. count reflects occupied slots. Completion can occur out of order; retirement stays in order, at most one per edge. Falling edges and stable clock input/reset-release changes hold all outputs; reset assertion immediately clears at either clock level.
Public ordered binary events (clk,rst_n,packed input,packed output; ports packed in listed order; sample after #2):
